  "narrative": "No assessments are due, and independent validation capacity is exhausted, so this explore stage registers focused discovery follow-ups rather than broad mining. The outcome is dependency_composite in composite dependency-score units, with more negative values meaning stronger dependency. Practical meaningful effects must exceed 0.15 units in the registered direction; for a main effect, acceptance will require the signed point estimate and the lower signed interval bound to exceed 0.15, and for a technical negative control any large batch difference would be informative even if the pre-registered direction is not specific. All returned estimates and intervals are already signed to the registered direction, so positive signed evidence supports a claimed positive or negative effect depending on the registered claim direction. The accepted dataset-specific marker associations remain: SMARCA4 loss and MSI-high mark stronger dependency; TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss mark weaker dependency; PTEN loss marks a moderate stronger-dependency association. The first two claims fill histology gaps by testing KEAP1 loss and SMARCA4 loss within adenocarcinoma. The expected KEAP1-loss direction is positive because KEAP1 loss has been associated with weaker dependency, whereas SMARCA4-loss expected direction is negative because SMARCA4 loss has been associated with stronger dependency. The third claim tests whether SMARCA4 loss remains associated with stronger dependency in cells without TP53 loss, KEAP1 loss, or MSI-high, reducing contamination from co-occurring strong markers. The fourth claim refines the unresolved CDKN2A investigation by testing CDKN2A loss in a larger Avana-library subset with adequate Cas9 activity and high screen-confidence filtering while excluding TP53, KEAP1, MSI-high, and SMARCA4 co-occurrence. CDKN2A is expected to be negative if it marks stronger dependency, but it has repeatedly been threshold-adjacent and sensitive to context and cell counts. The fifth claim refines PTEN quality filtering: PTEN loss is expected negative, and this pre-specified subset should have more cells than the very stringent prior PTEN claim while still requiring Avana library, high screen ROC, and adequate Cas9. The final claim is a technical negative-control comparison of screen batch A versus batch C; the anticipated direction is zero because batch effects should not represent biological dependency. Plausible alternatives in every new claim are no true effect, attenuation, opposite-direction effects, confounding by lineage, molecular co-occurrence, library, Cas9 activity, screen quality, or batch composition. These claims remain dataset-specific measured associations, not causal dependencies, mechanistic claims, single-gene knockout interpretations, or external generalizations.",
  "research_notes": "Current dataset-specific synthesis before the next analyses: robust accepted markers are SMARCA4 loss and MSI-high, both associated with stronger dependency; TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss, both associated with weaker dependency; and PTEN loss, a moderate stronger-dependency association. Key references: SMARCA4 H43/R40 signed +0.804 [0.742,0.867] with validation R65 +0.803 [0.712,0.894]; MSI-high H10/R10 signed +0.775 [0.664,0.885] with validation R92 +0.831 [0.668,0.993]; TP53 H11/R11 signed +0.829 [0.767,0.891] with validation R78 +0.771 [0.673,0.868]; KEAP1 H13/R7 signed +0.810 [0.745,0.875] with validation R52 +0.840 [0.754,0.926]; PTEN H8/R8 signed +0.239 [0.145,0.332] with validation R13 +0.294 [0.149,0.439]. Many molecular, lineage, technical, media, batch, omics-availability, research-marker, and interaction comparisons were rejected or remained threshold-adjacent. CDKN2A is the main unresolved biological marker: repeatedly point estimates are around 0.13-0.19 but interval lower bounds are often below 0.15 or below zero, and stringent contexts reduce precision. The newest CDKN2A claim H273 in Avana, Cas9 score >=0.9, core-negative including PTEN-negative cells gave signed +0.169 [0.091,0.247], supportive but not threshold-decisive. PTEN is accepted overall but high-quality stringency can weaken precision: H274 Avana, Cas9 >=0.9, screen_roc_auc >=0.95 gave signed +0.214 [0.062,0.367]. Interactions have not produced an accepted lower bound above 0.15; suggestive TP53-by-MYC, PTEN-by-MYC, and MSI-by-slow-growth results remain unresolved and should not be called supported effect modification. Independent validation capacity is exhausted, so this explore stage registers only discovery-level refinements: KEAP1 in adenocarcinoma, SMARCA4 in adenocarcinoma, SMARCA4 in TP53/KEAP1/MSI-negative context, CDKN2A in a broader high-quality core-negative Avana subset with lower Cas9 threshold 0.8 and screen ROC >=0.94, PTEN in Avana with screen ROC >=0.94 and Cas9 score >=0.8, and a screen_batch A-vs-C technical negative control. Acceptance criteria for all new claims require valid cells and signed lower interval bound above 0.15 in the claimed direction; batch control is not expected to show a meaningful biological difference. All conclusions remain dataset-specific associations."
